---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Ornament from '../../components/Ornament.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RelatedPages from '../../components/RelatedPages.astro';
import GetTheApp from '../../components/GetTheApp.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const title = 'CardHabit vs Finch: Card-Based vs Pet-Based Habit Tracker';
const description = 'CardHabit compared to Finch. Finch grows a virtual pet when you complete self-care tasks. CardHabit deals five habit cards every morning, and every finished card fills your binder. Different gamification: nurturing a pet vs collecting a deck.';

// Content last substantively changed: November 2026. Update by hand when the page changes.
const updated = 'November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Breadcrumbs section="Comparisons" name="CardHabit vs Finch" />
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section style="padding:5rem 1.5rem 3rem;text-align:center;">
      <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;">
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.28em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Comparison
        </p>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7vw,3.75rem);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.015em;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.75rem;">
          CardHabit <em style="color:#6E1E22;font-style:italic;">vs Finch.</em>
        </h1>
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;color:#574B40;max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;">
          Finch turned self-care into a beloved pet-care game with millions of installs. CardHabit takes a different angle on the same problem: both apps turn daily habits into a game, but they pull motivation from opposite places.
        </p>
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#645749;margin:1.5rem 0 0;">
          Updated {updated}
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Ornament />

    <section style="padding:3rem 1.5rem;">
      <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;color:#574B40;">
        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">The short version</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">Choose Finch if nurturing a small creature that depends on you sounds like the right motivational lever: soft, warm, low-pressure self-care gamified through pet ownership. Choose CardHabit if you'd rather be dealt a hand every morning, build a collection out of the days you showed up, and share cards with friends who play alongside you.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">At a glance</h2>

        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:0 0 2rem;">
          <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.95rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.35);">
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">Feature</th>
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">CardHabit</th>
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">Finch</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Platform</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">iOS</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">iOS, Android</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Motivational lever</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">A daily deal of five cards and a binder to fill</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Virtual pet care</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Tone</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Quiet, premium, a luxury card deck</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Soft, cozy, encouraging</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Social</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Deal a friend in: share a card, finish it together (2.0)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Limited (friend codes, gifting)</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Daily structure</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">5-card daily deal (five suits plus the Joker in 2.0)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">User-defined goals</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Free tier</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Yes (2 daily commits)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Yes (most features)</td></tr>
              <tr><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Premium</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Pro $4.99/mo or $39.99/yr (7-day trial)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">~$5.99/mo Finch Plus</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Where Finch wins</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">Finch is gentle by design. The pet care metaphor turns "I need to drink water" into "Finch is thirsty too", externalizing the motivation in a way that lowers the activation cost of self-care. The platform reach is also broader (Android + iOS), and the soft tone is right for people who bounce off discipline-coded apps.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">If your habit-app history is "I keep downloading these and they make me feel bad," Finch's nurturing frame is built for you.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Where CardHabit is different</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">CardHabit isn't soft, and it isn't extreme either. It deals you a hand of five habit cards every morning, you commit to what you can handle, and every card you finish goes into your binder. The aim is hard things every day, not extreme things once.</p>

        <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:1.4rem;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 0.5rem;">Friends share cards, not comments</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;">In Finch, a friend can send encouragement. In CardHabit 2.0, you can deal a friend in: say your friend Alex is holding a card for a screen-free evening. He deals the same card into your hand for today, by share link if you don't have the app yet. If you both finish it, you each get a paired foil card with both names on it in your binders. If one of you doesn't finish, nothing bad happens. It is an invitation, not a dare.</p>

        <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:1.4rem;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 0.5rem;">A binder instead of a pet to feed</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Finch's reward loop runs through the bird: complete tasks, the pet grows. CardHabit's reward loop runs through the deck. Every card you finish fills a slot in your binder, the collection the app calls the Codex, and rarer cards carry a richer printed finish, from plain to a foil edge to full gold foil. Rank and XP build quietly underneath. A paired foil card from a Wednesday you finished alongside a friend says more than a sticker.</p>

        <h3 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:1.4rem;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 0.5rem;">A deck you grow into, not a pet you name</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;">With CardHabit 2.0, the deck has five suits: Physical, Mind, Nutrition, Recovery, and Connection, plus the Joker, a wild card that can ask for anything. You don't choose which suits fill your binder first. The work you actually did decides that, and over time the binder shows which parts of your life you have been showing up for.</p>

        <p style="margin:0;">If Finch is a self-care companion, CardHabit is a daily card draw for your life, played alongside people you care about. Different frames for different temperaments.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Ornament />

    <RelatedPages current="/vs/finch" />

    <Ornament />

    <GetTheApp />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
